WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.270
So as we get into the middle of the week this
week, we are now really just five weeks from

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.370
the start of the first early ballots and absentee
ballots in various states.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:14.890
So I want to have sort of like a very sober
conversation with you so that we don't all

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:20.539
end up surprised and devastated on November
4th if Donald Trump wins.

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:22.730
We would obviously still be devastated.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.710
But I don't want us to be surprised, despite
all of the polling that we've been looking

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.410
at, these great polls for Joe Biden in states
nationally, etc., and we'll look at some of

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.410
them later.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.820
Donald Trump can still win reelection here.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.040
When you look at the historical precedent,
it looks really bad for Trump.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.910
When you look at being 100 days out in past
elections, no incumbent has been reelected

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:50.200
with this level of disapproval, combined with
the level of chaos in our country and in our

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.830
economy, like it looks historically disastrous
for Donald Trump.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.980
Trump can't get past 40 percent approval.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.140
Two thirds of the country thinks corona virus
is getting worse.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.360
Unemployment is at 11 percent.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.280
Trump is underwater in just about every battleground
state.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.780
Trump is mishandling the three most important
issues to voters today.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.400
Voters say the most important issues are corona
virus, economy and race relations.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.060
And they prefer Biden over Trump to different
degrees on those three issues.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.350
And yet Trump can win.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.670
Now, of course, we all know there could be
a so-called October surprise.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:26.530
And a lot of the questions I get about how
Trump could win are what kind of October surprise

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.390
could turn it around.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:33.520
OK, we get a cure and vaccine and Trump takes
credit for it and some people fall for it.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.939
Maybe Trump lies about coronavirus numbers
to justify reopening the economy and the economy

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:40.920
improves even if temporarily.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.539
And Trump gets credit, takes credit.

00:01:42.539 --> 00:01:46.119
OK, you know, Trump cures cancer or something
like that.

00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:51.350
Trump goes to war either with another country
or with law enforcement in Portland or Chicago,

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.880
as we are seeing.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.119
But the thing is, we don't actually even need
a so-called October surprise for Donald Trump

00:01:58.119 --> 00:01:59.119
to win.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:03.740
What can happen has a lot to do with us and
a lot to do with Donald Trump.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.860
So on their side, continued anger at.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.789
The way Trump has been treated, Trump has
argued he's the victim, he's just treated

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:12.370
so terribly.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:17.450
And some people will fall for it and they
could actually say, I'm going to turn out

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:22.760
because Trump has been treated so unfairly
only in some of those close key states.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.900
And Trump katik this out.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.160
I'm talking places like North Carolina, Pennsylvania,
Florida, places where there's certainly a

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.900
lead for Biden right now, but not necessarily
an overwhelming one.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.709
Then add to that that the polling could be
slightly too favorable to Joe Biden.

00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:41.819
So this is not the polls are wrong, but imagine
that the margin of error, which is there for

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:44.069
a reason, skews towards Donald Trump.

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:47.260
So when Biden is plus four, he's really plus
one right now.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.819
So if Biden's really plus one, you don't need
that much for it to be a Trump win by a small

00:02:51.819 --> 00:02:56.371
margin like we saw in a bunch of states in
2016 when Biden is plus three right now, maybe

00:02:56.371 --> 00:02:57.940
that's really a tie.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.500
And that could push this even closer.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.140
And then the left could do self-inflicted
damage to itself.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:07.500
I talked yesterday about, you know, let's
postpone some of the policy disagreements

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.250
that don't make a difference right now until
after the election.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.640
Let's focus on winning.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.950
As an example, I mentioned the debate between
Medicare for all and a public option, important

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.730
debate, significant debate, so important to
so many people's lives.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.290
But in the next three months, it doesn't do
anything for us.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:26.290
Biden is not in favor of Medicare for all.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.319
Most Senate Democrats aren't in favor of it.

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:32.209
And with Trump, we're not getting either Medicare
for all nor the public option.

00:03:32.209 --> 00:03:35.870
So what's the point of debating that for the
next three months when the focus should be

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.010
get out the vote?

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:41.410
The most important thing we can do is run
as if we're three points behind.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.920
I'm sorry.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.439
Run as if we're 10 points behind.

00:03:45.439 --> 00:03:50.140
But vote as if our vote could decide the states
in which we are voting.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:55.840
I know my vote's not going to decide Massachusetts,
but I'm operating in the mindset of my vote

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.150
is as important as it would be.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:05.420
I'm taking it as seriously as I would if Massachusetts
could go one vote to Trump or by one vote

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.670
to Joe Biden.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:12.440
If we all actually do this, we could end up
with a historic rebuke of the Republican Party,

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.739
not just the White House, but also the Senate.

00:04:14.739 --> 00:04:20.199
If we don't, the devastation on November 4th
is going to be overwhelming.

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:22.389
Vote early, vote absentee if you can.

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:24.560
I've already requested my absentee ballot.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:29.690
Consider the betting Web sites, which generally
tend to give Joe Biden about a 60 percent

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:31.039
chance of winning right now.

00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:36.020
Remember, Hillary on many Web sites had a
70 percent chance in 2016 and she lost.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:40.210
So Joe Biden having 60 percent means Trump
has 40 percent.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.919
Those aren't great odds for anybody to decide
to stay home.

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:47.000
If when I see those numbers, I don't say I'll
sit back and be an observer here.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.419
No, I'll be a participant.

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:50.419
So the messages Trump can win.

00:04:50.419 --> 00:04:51.419
Trump can win.

00:04:51.419 --> 00:04:52.430
Trump can win.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:57.240
No complacency, no smugness or satisfaction
from the polling data.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.870
The polling data is a signal that tells us
we have an opportunity.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.220
That's the way I see it.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.400
North Carolina looks like it's Biden plus
seven.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.020
I'll talk about that later.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.990
That means Biden has an opportunity in North
Carolina.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.509
That's the way we read the polling until Election
Day.

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:17.060
That's all the polling tells us, which is
why this has to be the message until November

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:18.110
3rd.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.780
Let me know your thoughts on Twitter at David
Pakman.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:06:58.430
We will take a very short break and be

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:05.620
right back.

